id:                     E374
trigger_tool: conan|buildbot|binary-sign-tool
phase: testing|consumer-runtime
error_signature: OHOS runtime execution requires signing tools: objcopy, readelf, signer
severity: 2
category:               detection, conan, runtime
match_keywords: Conan test_package, can_run, OHOS, binary-sign-tool, llvm-objcopy, llvm-readelf, compile link, runtime NOT_RUN, Buildbot
title: Separate Conan consumer compile-link proof from unavailable signed runtime execution
root_cause: Conan can_run() establishes build/host compatibility, but it does not prove that an OHOS worker has the complete ELF signing toolchain required to execute newly linked binaries. A same-OS worker can therefore compile and link a real consumer while being unable to safely execute that consumer or packaged commands.
affected_scope: Conan test_package recipes that build OHOS ELF consumers or commands on workers where build and host settings match but llvm-objcopy, llvm-readelf, or binary-sign-tool is absent.
verification_cmd: Run the production test() entry with complete artifacts and missing signing tools, missing consumer, missing command, a complete tool set, and can_run(false) positive/negative paths; require 7/7 directed cases and preserve the full runtime path when tools exist.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: artifact-first-capability-gated-runtime
rec_description: First require the linked consumer and every packaged command to exist. Resolve the complete signing tool set. If and only if a signing tool is absent, report runtime as NOT_RUN while retaining the truthful compile-link result; when tools exist, sign every runtime ELF and execute the original assertions. Missing artifacts, signing failures, command failures, and assertion failures remain fatal.
rec_command: validate consumer and command paths; resolve objcopy/readelf/signer; emit explicit NOT_RUN only for missing tools; otherwise sign and run
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: isolated-signed-device-runtime
fallback_description: Execute the unchanged runtime assertion set on an authorized target with task-private signed copies, and report it separately from CI compile-link evidence.
fallback_command: run the signed consumer and command matrix on one exact target snapshot
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual-device-validation
forbid_1_pattern: except Exception.*Runtime test skipped|can_run\(self\).*return.*pass|TARGET_RUNTIME_TESTS=PASS.*signing tools unavailable
forbid_1_reason: Broad exception handling or relabeling an unexecuted runtime as PASS hides package, signing, loader, and assertion regressions.
forbid_1_consequence: CI appears green without proving either valid artifacts or the intended target behavior.
forbid_2_pattern: skip.*before.*(consumer|command).*exists|missing command.*NOT_RUN
forbid_2_reason: Capability gating must happen only after compile-link output and packaged command presence are proven.
forbid_2_consequence: Missing or broken package artifacts are misclassified as an environment limitation.
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: [E077, E221, E230]
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
